# Surfshark

> Surfshark is a Netherlands-based cybersecurity company focused on privacy and security innovations and services (part of Nord Security since 2022). Surfshark offers digital privacy and cybersecurity solutions - a no-logs VPN with 4,500+ RAM only servers in 100 countries, supporting simultaneous device connections; antivirus software; personal data removal, and identity protection tools. The site (surfshark.com) is the primary commercial and educational hub: product and service pages, platform-specific download pages, feature deep-dives, pricing, blog content, original cybersecurity research, free online tools, and full support documentation.

Key facts:
- Headquartered in the Netherlands (zero logging mandates), this jurisdiction allows Surfshark to uphold strict no-logs policy with no interference.
- Strict no-logs policy, independently audited (Deloitte, Cure53). RAM-only server infrastructure (100% diskless).
- Protocols: Dausos (proprietary), WireGuard, OpenVPN, IKEv2.
- Industry-leading encryption: AEGIS-256X2, AES-256, ChaCha20
- Unlimited simultaneous connections per single subscription.
- 30-day money-back guarantee; 7-day free trial.
- 24/7 customer support via live chat.

Surfshark technology and innovations:
- Everlink: industry-first patented self-healing technology that keeps the VPN connection stable and secure by instantly restoring dropped connections.
- Post-quantum encryption: designed to resist potential threats from future quantum computers [available on Wireguard and Dausos protocols].
- AEGIS-256X2 encryption: cutting-edge cipher designed for high speed and strong security -  a new standard in personal cybersecurity.
- FastTrack: Routes traffic through a network of servers rather than a single VPN tunnel, boosting internet speeds.
- Auto-connect & Quick-connect: automatically establishes a VPN connection; connects to the fastest or chosen preferred location.
- GPS override: exclusively for Android devices that forces the device's GPS to match your chosen VPN server location.
- Reverse Bypasser: manually select apps and websites to send through the VPN tunnel, leaving the rest of your traffic VPN-free.
- Pause VPN: allows to stop VPN use for a limited time (on hold for 5min, 30min, or 2h).
- Website safety settings: blocks malware on websites. Notifies about leaks the webpage experienced in the past.

